+# Corpus fetching
+
+The corpus fetch had to respect Svipall's per-domain limit of **12 visits per
+60-second window**. After a breach, that domain entered a **900-second
+(15-minute) cooldown**. In practice, fetches were kept to batches of at most 12
+per domain, with at least 65 seconds between batches.
+
+The files were fetched through these CDN/mirror hosts:
+
+- `raw.githubusercontent.com`
+- `cdn.jsdelivr.net` (using `/gh/<owner>/<repo>@<branch>/<path>` URLs)
+- `cdn.statically.io` (this mirror was slow and sometimes timed out)
+
+The manifest independently identifies `raw.githubusercontent.com` as the raw
+source. The numeric limits and the two alternate mirrors are preserved in the
+project's recorded fetch-session history; no fetch script or configuration
+containing them is present in this checkout.
